From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t3code-customize <t3code-customize@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:50:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Local: proxy forecasts, subagents and panel link

- Usage page, wide layout: each account segment carries its week sparkline
  and a "next" badge on the account the proxy gives the next new chat, which
  the compact rows show as well.
- Forecasts: the proxy already sends each account's demand forecast. When it
  says a window runs dry before its reset, the thread card shows a Forecast
  row for the routed account, the segment popover a Forecast line, and the
  Usage notices name the account and when.
- Subagents fold into their parent chat per account, and the thread card
  shows how many ran and on which accounts.
- An "Open panel" card links to the proxy's management panel.
- A proxy on this machine without a configured label is called "CLI Proxy"
  instead of its address, matching the thread card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
